  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="5f67-d33c-299e-002d" name="Ancient Greek (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ANCIENT GREEK ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.14-15), the hoplite armies of Athens, Thebes and Sparta.
Characters: the army may have a General (no Army Standard Bearer). Cavalry up to a quarter of the points; Phalanx at least half; Light Infantry up to a quarter.
The Oracles: Greek armies may not have unit standards or Army Standard Bearers. Instead roll 1D6 per 1,000 points at the start of the battle; each point may add +1 to a combat resolution score (maximum +2) or re-roll a failed Leadership test once; once used it is spent.
Phalanxes: units of at least 16 models with a rank bonus of at least +1 fight as a phalanx (see the rule).

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Phalanx: at least 50%
  Light Infantry: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
